Third-party code and libraries
------------------------------

palette 0.7 (dev-dependency, tests only)
  https://github.com/Ogeon/palette
  MIT OR Apache-2.0
  Used as an independent check of the IEC 61966-2-1 sRGB transfer. The
  runtime curve lives in kagra-shared/src/render/color_space.rs and the
  WGSL shaders so the wasm and Android builds do not link this crate.

image 0.25 (jpeg and webp features only; default features off so rayon stays out)
  https://github.com/image-rs/image
  MIT OR Apache-2.0
  Decodes glTF JPEG (via zune-jpeg) and WebP (via image-webp). PNG stays
  on the png crate. The wasm and Android builds use these pure-Rust
  decoders.

image-webp (pulled by image's webp feature)
  https://github.com/image-rs/image-webp
  MIT OR Apache-2.0
  Lossless and lossy WebP decode for glTF images. No encoder in the runtime.

The Narkowicz ACES fit in bloom.wgsl and shader3d.wgsl is the public
approximation published by Krzysztof Narkowicz (2016), used widely
including by three.js (MIT). No three.js source is copied in this tree.
